   "tekst_poczatek": " --> Demystifying Sports Tipsters | Tipsto top of page Where opinions pay. tipsto Menu Close Home Resources Privacy policy Rules Terms of use Anton Hyberg &nbsp;- &nbsp;Apr 28 ​ ​ What is a Sports Tipster? ​ ​ Demystifying an Industry at the Intersection of Insight and Illusion ​ A sports tipster is someone who provides betting advice on the outcomes of sporting events. These tips can range from simple predictions (e.g., &ldquo;Manchester City to win&rdquo;) to more complex betting strategies involving odds, handicaps, or accumulators. &nbsp; A solid tipster usually understands and informs the customer/follower on the expected value (ie. how lucrative the bet is) and the estimated chance of winning. A sharp % probability estimation is a professional way to do this.&nbsp; &nbsp; Tipsters now operate across every platform imaginable &mdash; Twitter/X, Telegram, Discord, private forums, and purpose-built communities like OLBG and Blogabet. Some claim professional expertise or algorithmic edge. Others offer casual commentary or mimic insider knowledge. But with this growth has come a flood of misleading actors &mdash; and an increasing need for discernment. The Different Breeds of Tipsters &nbsp; The tipster world is anything but homogeneous. Here&rsquo;s a breakdown: ​ Free Tipsters: Found mostly on social media and on platforms such as Blogabet and Betrush. Many generate income through affiliate deals &mdash; they earn when users sign up and bet through their links. Transparenc",
